  "slug": "simulations-structural-6310",
  "summary": "Enhanced-sampling simulations now map multiple binding modes in full-length and disordered protein systems, with learned latent representations added to the analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is treating biomolecular binding as a conformational ensemble to be sampled rather than a single bound structure. Two preprints apply enhanced sampling to multimodal binding. For full-length CYFIP1-eIF4E, funnel-restrained TAMD on Martini 3 combined with beta-VAE latent-space clustering identifies three recurring binding modes. For the intrinsically disordered FCP1 region binding Rap74, OneOPES simulations reveal a multimodal conformational landscape with thermodynamic characterization and introduce a Divide et impera free-energy decomposition. What is new is the coupling of learned latent representations with physics-based sampling. The simulated annealing preprint on de novo sequence design via Topological Spatial Chunking addresses inverse folding rather than conformational ensembles and sits at the periphery of this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
